# patch: 009-compact-signal-chunked
# format: CHUNKED ONLY (2.1.242+). Monolithic keeps 009-compact-signal.patch.
# version: authored against 2.1.260
# depends: 002
# description: Mirrors {type:"compact"} at the post-compaction chokepoint.
#
# WHERE IT MOVED: bootstrap/sessionState.js still EXISTS on chunked but is a pure
#   re-export BARREL with no function bodies (see 001). markPostCompaction's real
#   body is `gtt` in vendor/lodash/memoizeCapped.js.
#
# IDENTITY IS PROVEN, NOT GUESSED. `gtt` is confirmed to be markPostCompaction by
#   the barrel's own export line `gtt as markPostCompaction,` in
#   bootstrap/sessionState.js — i.e. by upstream's export map as recovered by the
#   anchor pass, not by shape-matching. The remaining minified names (`n` for the
#   root-session getter) appear only in CONTEXT.
#
# UPSTREAM SIGNATURE CHANGE (handled, not carried over): on 2.1.238 the body was
#   the single line `ROOT_SESSION.requestJournal.replacePendingPostCompaction(!0);`.
#   It now takes `(e, { keepsCachedPrefix = !1 } = {})` and performs three journal
#   updates. The emit is placed at the END of the function so it fires after the
#   post-compaction state is fully written, matching the monolithic patch's intent
#   (mirror once compaction has been recorded) rather than its line position.
#   The anchored method name `replacePendingPostCompaction` is retained in context.
#
# ⚠️ NOT EXERCISED BY THE TURN TEST (a one-shot `-p` turn never compacts).
#   Applying and bundling are VERIFIED; live emission is BELIEVED.
#
# ============================================================================
# RE-AUTHORED 2026-09-07 — ANCHOR-DRIVEN, CROSS-VERSION VERIFIED
# ============================================================================
# STATUS: VERSION-INDEPENDENT (verified on 2.1.263 AND 2.1.260).
#
# WHAT CHANGED AND WHY THE OLD HUNK BROKE:
#   The old hunk used wide context that included the enclosing declaration
#   `function gtt(e, { keepsCachedPrefix: t = !1 } = {})` — and that name is a
#   bundler name (`crt` on 2.1.263). The statement the patch actually targets
#   is unchanged between builds.
#
# THE ANCHOR:
#   `        o.replaceLastMainThreadRequest(null, null);`
#   UNIQUE (1 occurrence) in both trees, verified by grep -c in each. It is a
#   METHOD call on the request journal — method names on this object survive
#   minification (they are real API surface), which is what makes it stable.
#   Context is that line plus the closing `}` of the function.
#
# MINIFIED NAME IN CONTEXT: `o` (the request-journal local). It appears ONLY
# on the context line, never on an added line, and that context line is what
# pins it. The added line references only `globalThis.__claudiverse`.
#
# NOTE: the hunk's line numbers were generated against a tree that also had
# 001 applied, so its @@ offsets are ~5 lines skewed from a pristine tree.
# git's normal offset search absorbs this — verified applying standalone to
# BOTH pristine trees. No renumbering was hand-edited into the body.
#
diff --git a/vendor/lodash/memoizeCapped.js b/vendor/lodash/memoizeCapped.js
index 0bae2c1..7ef81cc 100644
--- a/vendor/lodash/memoizeCapped.js
+++ b/vendor/lodash/memoizeCapped.js
@@ -4459,2 +4464,5 @@ function crt(e, { keepsCachedPrefix: t = !1 } = {}) {
         o.replaceLastMainThreadRequest(null, null);
+    try {
+        globalThis.__claudiverse.mirrorMessage({ type: 'compact' });
+    } catch (__e) {}
 }
